MAST taxonomy files, vendored for the ErrorProbe paper mode
============================================================

Source: https://github.com/multi-agent-systems-failure-taxonomy/MAST
        (folder taxonomy_definitions_examples/, fetched 2026-09-05)

Paper:  Mert Cemri et al., "Why Do Multi-Agent LLM Systems Fail?",
        arXiv:2503.13657 (NeurIPS 2025 Datasets and Benchmarks Track).

Files copied verbatim:
  taxonomy_definitions_examples/definitions.txt   the 14 failure-mode definitions
  taxonomy_definitions_examples/examples.txt      the authors' worked examples

Why they are here: baselines/errorprobe/paper/tagger.py builds its step-level
MAST tagger from the MAST authors' own LLM annotator (llm_judge_pipeline.ipynb
in the same repository), which hands the model these two files. The tagger
reads definitions.txt on every call and examples.txt only when
include_mast_examples is on.

License: the upstream repository showed no license file when these files were
fetched. They are reproduced here for research reproduction only; the
